    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0518" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg506"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/12–2144: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Representatives </hi><anchor n="91" xml:id="d447-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-21T00:00:00-04:00">December 21,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Barnes understands that all members of Muraviev Cabinet except Muraviev himself
                    and Dimov have been released but have signed pledges to appear before the
                    Peoples courts when called. This move is generally considered to mean that only
                    Dimov is in danger. It is generally believed that the Russians had been
                    persuaded not to take action against the other ministers since such action would
                    undermine the declaration of war against Germany which constituted the final
                    action of the Cabinet in question. War criminal trials will begin on December 21
                    and there is some fear that the penalties will be heavy and justice may not be
                    dispensed impartially. Those persons bearing the greatest responsibility for
                    Bulgarian participation in the war such as Filov, Gabrovsky<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d447-f2"/> and Prince Cyril are now imprisoned in Russia where they
                    will be held for trial by an international court.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d447-f1" n="91" type="source" xml:id="d447-f1-content">
                <p>The diplomatic representatives at London, Paris, Madrid, Lisbon, Bern, Cairo,
                    Ankara, and Stockholm.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d447-f2" n="92" xml:id="d447-f2-content">
                <p>Peter Gabrovski, Bulgarian Minister of Interior, February 1940—August 1943.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
